# Neon Pairs

Neon Pairs is an offline browser memory game. Read the [game specification](docs/README.md) for its behavior, appearance and accessibility requirements.

## Install and run

Use Node.js 26.12.1 and npm 11.20.0. Install the locked packages, then run the development server with:

```sh
npm ci
npm run dev
```

The required versions are pinned exactly in `package.json` and `package-lock.json`: React and React DOM 19.3.1, TypeScript 7.0.2, Vite 8.3.5, `@vitejs/plugin-react` 6.1.2, `vite-plugin-singlefile` 2.3.4, Vitest 5.0.5, Playwright 1.64.1, React type definitions 19.3.0, and Node type definitions 24.19.2.

## Commands

```sh
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run test:e2e
npm run build
npm run --silent replay -- PATH
```

The build checks both the browser and Node compiler projects before emitting `dist/index.html`. That file includes its JavaScript and CSS and can be opened directly from disk. `test:e2e` always builds first, then runs the Playwright journeys against the fresh output. For saved-preference checks, serve the game over local HTTP because browser storage may differ on a `file:` URL.

The replay command accepts a version 1 replay JSON file. A valid replay prints only its final snapshot JSON to stdout and exits successfully. An invalid file prints an error to stderr and exits nonzero.

## Core API

Pure game behavior lives under `src/game`; it does not read browser storage, clocks, DOM state or random sources.

- `parseBoardCode` and `createGame` validate a board code and create its deterministic deal. The parser is strict; callers trim user-entered board-code drafts before parsing.
- `activateCard`, `advanceGame` and `isWon` apply turns and logical active time to immutable game state.
- `encodeSnapshot` and `decodeSnapshot` serialize progress and validate imported data. Unfinished-import pause state belongs to the browser session.
- `replayGame` validates and runs timed actions through the same transition functions.

Board generation uses the version 1 Park–Miller algorithm. Snapshot and replay validators reject unknown object keys, invalid state and data beyond their byte and action limits. The board, its deck, and returned state records are read-only and frozen; transitions return a new state when an action changes the game.

## Browser implementation

`src/Game.tsx` composes the status panel, deal controls, reproduction tools and board. The session hook owns active time, visibility changes, imported-snapshot pause state, saved scores and deal replacement. The board module owns arrow-key navigation, focus scrolling, accessible card names and inline SVG faces. Browser preferences use the dedicated JSON keys `neon-pairs.grid-size.v1` and `neon-pairs.best-moves.v1`; other local storage keys are left untouched.

Cards mount face artwork only while revealed or matched. Hidden cards have a shared diamond back. The app has one polite live region for turn results and reproduction statuses.

## Compatibility evidence

The initial locked install succeeded with Node.js 26.12.1 and npm 11.20.0. `npm run typecheck`, `npm test` (15 unit tests), and `npm run build` pass. The build emits a single `dist/index.html` file.

A targeted offline smoke ran from `file:///work/dist/index.html` in Playwright 1.64.1 with Chromium 156.0.8078.4. It checked the initial closed-card name, the exact mismatch result and 800ms close, snapshot export and paused import, blocked card activation while paused, Resume focus, arrow movement, and a 16x16 board with 44px cards and an 806px internal scroll area at 360x800. The document stayed 360px wide, and the page made no HTTP requests. The full browser journeys, served-storage checks, accessibility-tree capture, large-layout matrix and grayscale face-sheet review are still pending. No screen reader was used; spoken output remains a user acceptance check.
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";
import { createGame, parseBoardCode } from "../board.ts";
import { encodeSnapshot, decodeSnapshot } from "../snapshot.ts";
import { activateCard, isWon } from "../transitions.ts";
import type { GameState, GridSize } from "../types.ts";
import { formatElapsedTime, makeFreshBoardCode } from "./clock.ts";
import type { GameSession, Notice } from "./contracts.ts";
import { readPreferences, saveBestScores, saveGridSize } from "./storage.ts";
import type { BestScores } from "./storage.ts";
import { useActiveClock } from "./useActiveClock.ts";
function initialDeal(size: GridSize): GameState {
  const state = createGame(makeFreshBoardCode(size));
  if (state === null) throw new Error("Unable to create the initial deal.");
  return state;
}

export function useGameSession(): GameSession {
  const [preferences] = useState(readPreferences);
  const [game, setGame] = useState(() => initialDeal(preferences.gridSize));
  const [paused, setPaused] = useState(false);
  const [bestScores, setBestScores] = useState<BestScores>(preferences.bestScores);
  const [dealRevision, setDealRevision] = useState(0);
  const [celebration, setCelebration] = useState(false);
  const [notice, setNotice] = useState<Notice>({ text: "", revision: 0 });
  const gameRef = useRef(game);
  const pausedRef = useRef(false);
  const bestScoresRef = useRef(bestScores);
  const visibleRef = useRef(true);
  const dealRevisionRef = useRef(0);

  function updateGame(next: GameState): void {
    gameRef.current = next;
    setGame(next);
  }

  const clock = useActiveClock(gameRef, pausedRef, visibleRef, updateGame);

  function announce(text: string): void {
    setNotice((current) => ({ text, revision: current.revision + 1 }));
  }

  function tickAt(now: number): GameState {
    return clock.tickAt(now);
  }

  useEffect(() => {
    visibleRef.current = !document.hidden;
    if (!visibleRef.current) clock.suspend();
    let active = true;
    const revision = dealRevision;
    const isCurrentDeal = () => active && dealRevisionRef.current === revision;
    function onVisibilityChange(): void {
      if (!isCurrentDeal()) return;
      const now = performance.now();
      if (document.hidden) {
        if (visibleRef.current) tickAt(now);
        visibleRef.current = false;
        clock.suspend();
      } else {
        visibleRef.current = true;
        const current = gameRef.current;
        if (!pausedRef.current && current.started && !isWon(current)) clock.resumeAt(now);
      }
    }
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", onVisibilityChange);
    const timer = window.setInterval(() => {
      if (isCurrentDeal()) tickAt(performance.now());
    }, 50);
    return () => {
      active = false;
      window.clearInterval(timer);
      document.removeEventListener("visibilitychange", onVisibilityChange);
      clock.suspend();
    };
  }, [dealRevision]);

  function replaceDeal(next: GameState, nextPaused: boolean): void {
    updateGame(next);
    pausedRef.current = nextPaused;
    setPaused(nextPaused);
    clock.reset();
    setCelebration(false);
    dealRevisionRef.current += 1;
    setDealRevision(dealRevisionRef.current);
    saveGridSize(next.board.size);
  }

  function startCode(code: string): void {
    const next = createGame(code);
    if (next !== null) replaceDeal(next, false);
  }

  function newGame(): void {
    const current = gameRef.current;
    startCode(makeFreshBoardCode(current.board.size, current.board.seed));
  }

  function restart(): void {
    const current = gameRef.current;
    startCode(current.board.code);
  }

  function changeSize(size: GridSize): void {
    if (gameRef.current.board.size === size) return;
    const current = gameRef.current;
    startCode(makeFreshBoardCode(size, current.board.seed));
  }

  function publishStatus(text: string): void {
    announce(text);
  }

  function loadBoard(draft: string): boolean {
    const parsed = parseBoardCode(draft.trim());
    if (parsed === null) {
      publishStatus("Invalid board code.");
      return false;
    }
    startCode(parsed.code);
    publishStatus("Board loaded.");
    return true;
  }

  function loadSnapshot(draft: string): boolean {
    const restored = decodeSnapshot(draft);
    if (restored === null) {
      publishStatus("Invalid snapshot.");
      return false;
    }
    const completed = isWon(restored);
    replaceDeal(restored, !completed);
    publishStatus(completed ? "Loaded completed snapshot." : "Loaded snapshot. Select Resume to continue.");
    return true;
  }

  function exportSnapshot(): string {
    tickAt(performance.now());
    publishStatus("Snapshot exported.");
    return JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(encodeSnapshot(gameRef.current)), null, 2);
  }

  function resume(): void {
    if (!pausedRef.current || isWon(gameRef.current)) return;
    pausedRef.current = false;
    setPaused(false);
    clock.resumeAt(performance.now());
    publishStatus("Game resumed.");
  }

  function saveBestIfBeaten(won: GameState): void {
    const size = won.board.size;
    const previous = bestScoresRef.current[size];
    if (previous !== undefined && won.moves >= previous) return;
    const next = { ...bestScoresRef.current, [size]: won.moves };
    bestScoresRef.current = next;
    setBestScores(next);
    saveBestScores(next);
  }

  function activate(index: number): void {
    if (pausedRef.current || !visibleRef.current) return;
    const now = performance.now();
    const beforeTick = gameRef.current;
    if (beforeTick.started) tickAt(now);
    const before = gameRef.current;
    const next = activateCard(before, index);
    if (next === before) return;
    if (!before.started && next.started) {
      clock.begin(now);
    }
    updateGame(next);
    if (before.selection.kind === "one" && next.selection.kind === "mismatch") {
      announce("No match. Cards close after a short pause.");
    } else if (before.selection.kind === "one" && next.selection.kind === "closed") {
      if (isWon(next)) {
        setCelebration(true);
        saveBestIfBeaten(next);
        announce(`Pair found. All pairs found in ${next.moves} moves and ${formatElapsedTime(next.elapsedMs)}.`);
        clock.suspend();
      } else {
        const pairs = next.matched.length / 2;
        announce(`Pair found. ${pairs} ${pairs === 1 ? "pair" : "pairs"} matched.`);
      }
    }
  }

  return {
    game, paused, dealRevision, celebration, bestScores, notice,
    activate, newGame, restart, changeSize, loadBoard, loadSnapshot, exportSnapshot, resume,
  };
}
import { useRef } from "react";
import type { MutableRefObject } from "react";
import { advanceGame, isWon } from "../transitions.ts";
import type { GameState } from "../types.ts";

export type ActiveClock = Readonly<{
  tickAt: (now: number) => GameState;
  reset: () => void;
  begin: (now: number) => void;
  suspend: () => void;
  resumeAt: (now: number) => void;
}>;

export function useActiveClock(
  gameRef: MutableRefObject<GameState>,
  pausedRef: MutableRefObject<boolean>,
  visibleRef: MutableRefObject<boolean>,
  commit: (game: GameState) => void,
): ActiveClock {
  const lastTimeRef = useRef<number | null>(null);
  const fractionalMsRef = useRef(0);

  function tickAt(now: number): GameState {
    const current = gameRef.current;
    if (!visibleRef.current || pausedRef.current || !current.started || isWon(current)) {
      lastTimeRef.current = null;
      return current;
    }
    const last = lastTimeRef.current;
    if (last === null) {
      lastTimeRef.current = now;
      return current;
    }
    const elapsed = now - last + fractionalMsRef.current;
    const wholeMs = Math.floor(elapsed);
    fractionalMsRef.current = elapsed - wholeMs;
    lastTimeRef.current = now;
    if (wholeMs > 0) {
      const next = advanceGame(current, wholeMs);
      if (next !== current) commit(next);
      return next;
    }
    return current;
  }

  return {
    tickAt,
    reset() {
      lastTimeRef.current = null;
      fractionalMsRef.current = 0;
    },
    begin(now) {
      lastTimeRef.current = now;
      fractionalMsRef.current = 0;
    },
    suspend() {
      lastTimeRef.current = null;
    },
    resumeAt(now) {
      const current = gameRef.current;
      lastTimeRef.current = current.started && !isWon(current) && visibleRef.current ? now : null;
    },
  };
}
